I've played this game since release and I gotta say. It's amazing. I've stopped before it became F2P because of the Attunament quest for raids, as many others did. Im coming back now and I'm amazed with how much better the game is. It was always fun but now it's a whole new level of fun!
It has something for everyone, the housing is amazing, leveling is fun even though it might take a bit of time to do it.
The game had poor design choices at release and that's why it's not as popular as it should be.
It is almost fully voice acted, the voice acting is fantastic, funny and very entertaining. The community is very helpful and you can be darn certain that you'll have plenty to do!
Pros:
+ Beautiful world with lots to explore; (And exploring is rewarding)
+ Combat is fluid, dynamic and fast paced;
+ Choose your path! Explore, be a Scientist, or maybe a Soldier... How about a Settler! Each path will give you an extra way to play the game, be it rescuing and assassinating as a Soldier, researching and solving puzzles as a Scientist, taming the land and building settlements that benefit everyone as a Settler or exploring the land and it's hidden treasures as an Explorer!
+ You can buy or unlock things for your account by simply playing the game and everything in the cash shop is flair, no P2W ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥t no content lock;
+ Classes feels different and you're able to adjust your class to your playstyle. Two players with the same class might have totally different builds;
+ Art Style and Concept is just fantastic;
+ An absurd amount of quests that are story driven and fun;
+ Casual friendly but with very hardcore content for those daring adventurers;
+ Crafting is fun and you feel like you have control over what you're making;
+ Gathering is also fun with a lot of surprises depending on what type of gatherer you are!
+ Seasonal events are actually good!
+ BGM is incredible;
+ Basically anything you do in-game will be fun!
Cons:
- Each race can only be certain classes (Except humans, they can pick any class);
- Some bugs are still being overlooked;
- There is nearly zero marketing for the game. NCSoft, please stop neglecting this amazing game...
Don't believe me? Just go ahead and play it. You'll have a good time! :D

