Wurm Unlimited may very well be the game I looked for my entire gaming life; it is, without any doubt, the most complete sandbox game I ever player - it has amazing terraforming, building and crafting, all these while fighting to survive in a harsh medieval world. While I'm very well aware that this is not for everyone, for the right people it can absolutely be a 10 out of 10 game.
Pros:
- Totally terraformable world - you can raise, lower or flat the land, create mines or even strip down a whole mountain or raise a island in the middle of the ocean;
- Totally customizable buildings - a small hut or a huge castle, you can create them all, wall by wall, just the way you want (no predefined buildings, so only imagination is your limit);
- Really complex crafting system - you need to make the parts first (like nails, planks and shafts), combine them, then improve the items to the desired quality;
- You can choose to play on your own local server (which is really simple to set up and requires absolutely no technical knowledge), on any private server in the world or on the official MMO servers maintained by developers ;
- Fully moddable and customizable, which offers you, as a player, an unlimited number of extra options to play the game just the way you want.
Cons:
- Steep learning curve - it's really not the kind of game to "learn by playing casually"; it will most likely require you to spend quite a lot time "studying" on the wiki what and how you can do;
- Even on private servers, Wurm remains a grinding game; it is the kind of the game where results are not achieved in hours, days or even weeks, but months and years;
- Graphics are quite low quality and not on par with an AAA game from nowadays;
- It runs on Java, so you must have that installed on your computer (not that this is necessarily a bad thing).
If you used to love to play Minecraft or build castles out of lego blocks when you were a kid, and now want to "move to the next level", then you will totally love Wurm Unlimited, because it offers you just the same freedom, but with a lot of extra perks. It is really the kind of game you can play for years and never get bored of it.
On the other hand, is not a game for everyone - if you are into fancy graphics, fast action, immersive story, easy and relaxing games which you can finish in a week or a month, then Wurm Unlimited is definitely not the game for you and, if you'll buy it, you'll end up being really dissapointed.

0.64.1 Beta review!
TL;DR: Awesome grinder, grab it! But it has no online multiplayer, only hotseat.
-------------------
Pros:
+ Will run on a potato laptop;
+ Can use WASD or mouse to move;
+ Easy to learn;
+ Nice sound and music;
+ Different skills for each characters;
+ Plenty of possible skill builds;
+ Has loot filter options;
+ Has random portals (like Vaal Areas in PoE);
