I bought this game when it was first released and played from day one. After a month, the game lost most of it's players due to the one major reason: it was way too hardcore.
Honestly, if you just wanted to log in to run some dungeons, do some quests with friends and have fun, you would be disappointed. Dungeons, even the low level ones, were nerve breaking. You needed a lot of skill to even finish ONE and usually you would waste at least 2 hours trying. Raids needed 40 people to do and you had to do a long attunement quest to even be able to run content. There was no lvl 50 casual content at ALL.  Well, to summarize, they wanted the game to be way too hard and thus lost most of the player base.
But, the game also had a lot of good features:
- Awesome cartoonish graphics;
- Beautiful places and cities;
- Very good combat system without tab locking;
- Housing;
- Nice lore and quests;
- Great class and path system (yeah, you choose a class and also what is called a path);
- Nice crafting;
- Great overall gaming systems (UI, skill response, npc reaction, object interaction, etc).
Unfortunately, due to the aforementioned, I decided to stop playing, since it wasn't a game for me (not a hardcore player). And now, after a long time, since it became F2P, I decided to give it a try. And what I found surprised me. The content has been toned down to made it available and fun to both casual and semi hardcore players. Most of the mistakes Carbine did at launch were fixed:
- There are plenty of casual content, both low level AND at level cap;
- The game is not as grind as it used to be;
- Content were nerfed, to make it easier and fun (dungeons, raids, events, etc);
- Raids now need only 20 people;
- The attunement, although still needed, is way easier to complete;
- What was good is... better (bugs were fixed, graphics were optimized, etc);
So, I have to admit I am enjoying the game a lot more now. So, I do recommend the game, though I also have to say the population is really small right now, so it's kinda hard to find people to do low level content. If this is not a problem for you, then definitely give this game a try. I think you will have a blast.
Edit: Just a very important information I forgot. I am playing F2P right now, no subscription nor have spent any money on the game. It's perfect possible to play without using any real money.

