I've played around with many MMO's over the years, spent about a decade in Anarchy Online, Rift from Beta until 2016 and tried, spent time in many others along the way;
(RiP), AC2 (who remembers AC2?) etc, etc.   And so far WIldstar is everything you expect from a MMO with a lot of things that are unexpected and refreshing (some good, some bad...more a matter of taste).   Im still fairly new so I cant speak on some aspects but what I have seen has sucked me in questing(never been a fan of questing) crafting, small team instances, the housing is well done and functional with gardens, private mines, neigbors. There are a lot of 'pop up' adventures, random things to keep it fresh.  Ill check back with this after I reach 'endgame' but from what ive seen the endgame is fully fleshed out with many world bosses, veteran dungeon/instances, raids, large scale PvP.
I recommend any MMO fan to give this a whirl, the price is right(free to play), the cash store is hardly noticable and quality of life/cosmetic only and can be skipped entirely with in game currency.
